Z||000000||theogre||09-08-2001||08:06 PM||||GM revised the crank pulley on later model 2.5l. In fiero this applies to the 87-88 4 cyl. I've also listed the U vin version of the 4 cyl for those that may have aquired one thru an engine swap.<P>GM revised the timing gears to be sold as a mated set. Previously they were available individually. Always replace the timing gears as a set no matter where you get them.<P>[My notes in square brackets]<P>"It is also recomended that a crankshaft torsional damper [AKA Harmonic Balancer] be installed along with the [timing] gear set. The damper reduces critical crankshaft vibrations thereby decreasing [gear set] wear. When the new damper is installed, the old crankshaft pulley may be discarded. If the engine already has a damper, it should be reinstalled."<P>Source: GM TSB 90-6-21 Servicing Camshaft/Crankshaft Gears (Install Torsional Damper)<P>VIN	year	gear#	damp#<BR>R V 2	77-86	10101790	N/A Use Original<BR>R	87-90	10101790	10101369<BR>U	85-86	10101789	10112485<BR>U	87-89	10101789	10124651<P>I've given both the GM timing set number and the damper number. I don't know what the damper costs. I have found it in inventory for the 87+ R motor, so it's still out there.<P>Harmonic Balancers are just plane good for the motor. They reduce gear and bearing wear.<P>------------------<BR><I><B>Screamin Yellow Zonkers... If it's Screamin and Yellow, I ain't eatin it.</B></I>||||reg||6
